1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:16,914
I am the conscience. I review what you write for equity, diversity, inclusion and decolonization, and I hand back the fixed text. A grant, a paper, a course outline, an ethics application, a study plan: anything with people in it.

2
00:00:17,299 --> 00:00:28,709
Three examples. A grant application: I check its sex- and gender-based analysis, SGBA plus, which the health funders require, and the equity rules of the funder you are applying to.

3
00:00:28,709 --> 00:00:41,605
A course outline: I check it for decolonization. Whose perspectives are taught, whether Indigenous peoples are named as the specific nations concerned or flattened into one word, which voices are missing.

4
00:00:41,605 --> 00:00:57,959
A paper: I check the language for exclusion, and who the study includes and leaves out, with a number where one exists. Every time, I quote the exact line, cite a source for the finding, and hand back a rewritten passage you can paste in.

5
00:00:58,349 --> 00:01:13,057
About a community, I use what that community has published about itself, and I say where that stops; I never speak for one. When nothing is built yet, I return a design instead: who is included, who is asked, whose risk is named.

6
00:01:13,057 --> 00:01:26,902
I edit your file only when you ask me to apply the changes. My findings rest on the centre's curated resources, chosen for its region; the bookworm adds to them when I find a gap.

7
00:01:27,299 --> 00:01:32,626
A real run, on a made-up Participants paragraph. A member asks for a review.

8
00:01:32,626 --> 00:01:48,719
My answer is Flagged: the draft calls an English-only cohort from one clinic representative of Canada. Each finding quotes the line and names its source, and a closing list says what I could not back up, for the bookworm to find.

9
00:01:49,099 --> 00:02:03,888
Say what the document is and what you want checked: a grant's SGBA plus section, a course outline for decolonization, or a paper's language. The document types are examples; the review is the same.

10
00:02:04,299 --> 00:02:18,542
To use me, ask Claude Code for the conscience and point me at a section, a grant or a course outline. The first line is my verdict: OK or Flagged for a review, Designed for a plan, or Gap when I cannot deliver.

11
00:02:18,542 --> 00:02:31,988
I draw on a curated list of resources chosen for the centre's region. The bookworm can propose additions to the centre's list, such as a funder's equity guidance, and a person approves each one.
